      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hart Minnich and John Hufbauer officially founded Derby on July 11, 1871, filing the town's first plat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.derbyks.gov/314/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Derby Historical Society & Museum, housed in a 1923‑24 school building, showcases the town’s heritage on the National Historic Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://derbykshistorymuseum.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Derby’s public library began in 1957, moved to a dedicated building in 1968, and opened a modern facility in 2009 after a sales‑tax vote.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        24,
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.derbyks.gov/314/History",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 2011, the city repurposed the old library into a Welcome Center, featuring the Austin Room honoring long‑time residents Sam and Phyllis Austin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
